# Packaged datasets and configuration are checksummed by snapshot_manifest.toml
# (sha256 over the bytes), so their line endings must stay stable on every
# platform: force LF in the repository and in working trees.
*.csv text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# Notebooks in notebooks/ are committed WITH their executed outputs, on purpose.
#
# The repository's git rules otherwise call for nbstripout, and stripping is the
# right default for notebooks used as working scratch. These six are different:
# they are the reader-facing deliverable. They are read on GitHub, which executes
# nothing, so a stripped notebook is a wall of code with no results and the
# artifact loses its entire point.
#
# tests/test_notebook_hygiene.py enforces that the outputs are actually present,
# and that they are reproducible: no wall-clock reads, no unseeded generators, no
# network calls. That is what makes committing outputs safe here rather than a
# source of diff noise.
#
# Do not "fix" this by enabling the filter.
notebooks/*.ipynb -filter -diff
